<title>GREECE: ATHENS BROKERS PONDER HALTING TRADE IN PROTEST.</title>
<headline>ATHENS BROKERS PONDER HALTING TRADE IN PROTEST.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brokers at the Athens bourse, angered by the failure of the clearing house to settle with some brokerages on Thursday, held a floor meeting at Friday's open to decide whether to boycott trade, brokers said.</p>
<p>The general share index was stuck at Thursday's 918.12 close with no trading going on during the meeting.</p>
<p>&quot;We are holding a meeting at this point. We should take a decision on trading today shortly,&quot; a floor broker told Reuters by telephone.  </p>
<p>Athens bourse member firm Delta Securities was barred from trading on Thursday for non-compliance with settlement regulations. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
